From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Satoshi Ikeuchi <satosan.ikm@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: read split-PHY topology when OTP is unset

QCN9274 hw2.0 needs the single- or dual-MAC selection before target
capabilities can be queried. A zero or erased OTP board ID cannot describe
the topology, so the driver currently defaults to single MAC.

Use the radio's qcom,split-phy property for this otherwise ambiguous case.
This describes the individual device, without matching a machine name or
changing the default for other radios on the same system.

Keep valid OTP authoritative and retain the existing fallback for devices
without the property and for other hardware revisions. Leave later QMI
capability discovery and WMI mode selection unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/af9bc78d14fbe77db6e7526efaced162060f27bc
Signed-off-by: Satoshi Ikeuchi <satosan.ikm@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/msi.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
 
 #include "core.h"
@@ -209,8 +210,11 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pc
 		board_id = u32_get_bits(board_id, OTP_BOARD_ID_MASK);
 
 		if (!board_id || (board_id == OTP_INVALID_BOARD_ID)) {
+			dualmac = ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW20 &&
+				  device_property_read_bool(ab->dev, "qcom,split-phy");
 			ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_BOOT,
-				   "failed to read board id\n");
+				   "invalid OTP, selecting %s-mac\n",
+				   dualmac ? "dual" : "single");
 		} else if (board_id & OTP_VALID_DUALMAC_BOARD_ID_MASK) {
 			dualmac = true;
 			ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_BOOT,
